<h3>Iterations Before Test Error</h3>

<p>
"Iterations Before Test Error" is the number of iterations that are performed 
before the code checks for convergence.  It is important that this number not 
be excessively large so that overiteration does not occur.  When using with 
MAXIET algorithm this number will typically need to be 10 or larger so that
the program does not halt on the initial exit of MAXIET.
</p>

